---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const pages = [
  { href: `${base}/docs/intent-engineering/`, title: 'Intent Engineering', color: '#cba6f7', body: 'The discipline this workstation is built for: five claims about working above the editor, and the mechanism where each one becomes something a directory can prove.' },
  { href: `${base}/docs/how-it-works/`, title: 'How it works', color: '#89b4fa', body: 'The line, stage by stage: capture, refine, briefs, queue, implement, verify. Then the six mechanisms that stop living in the operator, each with the surface that implements it.' },
  { href: `${base}/docs/architecture/`, title: 'Architecture', color: '#cba6f7', body: 'Three planes. State is a file, not a claim. Why there is no database, no server and no account, and what that buys.' },
  { href: `${base}/docs/evidence/`, title: 'Evidence', color: '#d4af37', body: 'The ledger, the scoreboard, the paper trail a task leaves behind, one run end to end, and the software shipped through the line.' },
  { href: `${base}/docs/vocabulary/`, title: 'Vocabulary', color: '#94e2d5', body: 'Every named thing in Continuum, defined once: signal, brief, mode, gate, receipt, NEEDS YOU, ledger, scoreboard, regent, governor, substrate, gradient.' },
  { href: `${base}/docs/gradients/`, title: 'Gradients', color: '#a6e3a1', body: 'The open-source behavioral standards layer: arché, shodo, kinhin, zazen. The part of Continuum you can run today.' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Continuum, in full"
  eyebrow="Docs"
  color="#d4af37"
  intro="The landing page is the short answer. This is the long one: how the line runs, what it is made of, and how to check it."
>
  <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-14">
    {pages.map((p) => (
      <a href={p.href} class="glass-card p-5 flex flex-col gap-2 group">
        <span class="eyebrow" style={`color:${p.color};`}>{p.title}</span>
        <p class="text-[0.8125rem] text-text-muted">{p.body}</p>
        <span class="mt-auto pt-1 font-mono text-[0.625rem] text-text-dim group-hover:text-text-muted">read →</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="glass-card p-6 mb-14">
    <span class="eyebrow block mb-3" style="color:#f38ba8;">Compared to</span>
    <p class="text-[0.875rem] text-text-muted max-w-[680px]">
      Cursor, Claude Code and Copilot write the code. Devin, Factory and OpenHands run the
      task and report back that it is done. Continuum does not compete with either: it
      writes the task they run, keeps the state in your git instead of their sandbox, and
      refuses to take their word for done until the commit is on your remote. Five Claude
      Code sessions in tmux do the same work with you as the scheduler; that is the
      comparison that matters.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-text-dim">
    Questions people ask before they ask: on the <a href={`${base}/#faq`} class="text-text-muted hover:text-text-primary">landing page →</a>
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
